["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>An unregistered quad, a loaded rifle on the rack or a ride into a closed area each cost more than the hunt. Learn the rules once.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ATV\">ATV</button> (all terrain vehicle) means your quad. <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ORV\">ORV</button> (Off Road Vehicle) is the law's wider word <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: about this session</summary><ul><li>Most lines here were read directly in the official synopsis, the Off Road Vehicle Act and its regulation, and ICBC (Insurance Corporation of British Columbia) pages. Those lines show 95% or more.</li><li>ATV means a quad here. ORV is the law's wider word: quads, dirt bikes, side by sides and snowmobiles <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Your ATV's registration status is unknown. The checklist at the end sorts that out.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Three sets of rules for your ATV. Off Road Vehicle Act: registration, plate, helmet, lights, on Crown land and resource roads. Motor Vehicle Act through ICBC: licence, insurance and permits for public roads. Wildlife Act in the Synopsis: no loaded guns on it, no shooting from it, closed areas, everywhere you hunt.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Three sets of rules</text>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"38\" width=\"124\" height=\"256\" rx=\"10\"/><rect x=\"138\" y=\"38\" width=\"124\" height=\"256\" rx=\"10\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"38\" width=\"124\" height=\"256\" rx=\"10\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M30 120 L68 70 L106 120 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><path d=\"M40 120 Q 68 100 96 120\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <rect x=\"166\" y=\"80\" width=\"68\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><path d=\"M200 84 v32\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"306\" y=\"74\" width=\"52\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"332\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Regs</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"68\" y=\"146\">Off Road</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"164\">Vehicle Act</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"146\">Motor</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"164\">Vehicle Act</text>\n    <text x=\"332\" y=\"146\">Wildlife Act</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"164\">(Synopsis)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"68\" y=\"196\">Plate, helmet,</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"214\">lights, ID</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"252\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Crown land,</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"270\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">FSRs</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"196\">Licence,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"214\">insurance,</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"232\">permits</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Public roads</text>\n    <text x=\"332\" y=\"196\">No loaded gun,</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"214\">no shooting,</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"232\">closed areas</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"262\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Everywhere</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>FSR (Forest Service Road) = Crown land: the ORV (Off Road Vehicle) Act applies <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Private land: only with the owner's consent <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the table and the fine print</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Law</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Where it applies</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Off Road Vehicle Act and Regulation</td><td>Registration, plate, helmet, lights, photo ID (identification), kids <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td><td>Crown land, including resource roads <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Motor Vehicle Act, through ICBC</td><td>Licence, insurance and permits for any ride on or across a public road <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td><td>Public roads and highways</td></tr><tr><td>Wildlife Act, in the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</button></td><td>Loaded firearms on a conveyance, shooting from a vehicle, Motor Vehicle Closed Areas <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td><td>Everywhere you hunt</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>The ORV Act does not apply on a highway as defined in the Motor Vehicle Act <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Section 3.</li><li>A Forest Service Road (<button class=\"term\" data-term=\"FSR\">FSR</button>) is Crown land, not a highway, so the ORV Act applies there <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Most gravel roads are FSRs. A few gravel roads are highways. Ask the district office if unsure <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>No ORV on private land without the consent of the owner, lessee or occupant <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Section 17.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Registering your ATV with ICBC. One time fee of 48 dollars for plate and registration. The plate or sticker goes on the front, back or left side, flat and readable. Carry a copy of the registration. Riding unregistered on Crown land: 230 dollar fine.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Register once, plate on</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(130 130) scale(2.2)\"><rect x=\"-40\" y=\"-18\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"-46\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-6 -18 l6 -14 h10\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"200\" y=\"78\" width=\"40\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ORV</text>\n  <text x=\"246\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">front, back or left</text>\n  <g font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"196\" width=\"120\" height=\"84\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#fff\">$48</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"258\" fill=\"#fff\">one time</text>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"196\" width=\"120\" height=\"84\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Carry the</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"252\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">registration</text>\n    <rect x=\"270\" y=\"196\" width=\"120\" height=\"84\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#fff\">$230</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">unregistered</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Register with ICBC (Insurance Corporation of British Columbia) at any Autoplan broker <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: fees, transfers, plate rules</summary><ul><li>Since 1 November 2015 an ORV used on Crown land must be registered with ICBC and display its plate or sticker <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Registration is a one time fee of $48 for plate and registration combined <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. The regulation lists $30 registration plus $18 plate or sticker <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Register at any ICBC Autoplan broker <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Buying a used quad: register the transfer within 10 days, $28 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Plate or sticker goes on the front, back or left side, horizontal, clean and readable <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Carry a copy of the certificate of registration on the quad or on you. Show it to an officer on request <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Fine for an unregistered ORV on Crown land: $230 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where are you riding? On a Forest Service Road: valid driver's licence and at least 200,000 dollars third party liability insurance. Other Crown land: liability insurance recommended. On or along a public road: ICBC Basic insurance, licence decal and a driver's licence, plus a police permit unless just crossing at a stop sign or light.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"10\" width=\"240\" height=\"40\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Where are you riding?</text>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"68\" y2=\"72\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"72\"/><line x1=\"260\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"332\" y2=\"72\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"74\" width=\"124\" height=\"216\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"68\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">Forest</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"118\" fill=\"#fff\">Service Road</text>\n    <text x=\"68\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#fff\">Driver's</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"178\" fill=\"#fff\">licence</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"210\" fill=\"#fff\">$200,000</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"228\" fill=\"#fff\">liability</text><text x=\"68\" y=\"246\" fill=\"#fff\">insurance</text>\n    <rect x=\"138\" y=\"74\" width=\"124\" height=\"216\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">Other</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"118\" fill=\"#fff\">Crown land</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#fff\">Insurance</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#fff\">recommended</text>\n    <rect x=\"270\" y=\"74\" width=\"124\" height=\"216\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n    <text x=\"332\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">Public</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"118\" fill=\"#fff\">road</text>\n    <text x=\"332\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">ICBC Basic,</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">decal, licence</text>\n    <text x=\"332\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">Police permit,</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">unless crossing</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">at a stop sign</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\">or light</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>FSR (Forest Service Road): driver's licence and <strong>$200,000</strong> liability insurance <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact rules and ICBC classes</summary><ul><li>On an FSR: a valid driver's licence and at least $200,000 third party liability insurance, from ICBC or another insurer <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><p>\"While travelling on a Forest Service Road, operators of ATVs are required to hold a valid driver's licence and carry a minimum of $200,000 third-party liability insurance.\" Synopsis page 9 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</p><ul><li>On other Crown land: liability insurance is voluntary but recommended <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>On or across a public road: the quad needs ICBC Basic insurance and a licence decal, and you need a driver's licence <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>ICBC rate class 036 Basic covers highway operation only. It does not cover you on Crown land or FSRs <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Crossing a highway at a stop sign or traffic light, or loading in a parking lot: no police permit needed if the quad is licensed and insured <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Any other road riding needs a free police operation permit from the nearest detachment <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Buy the $200,000 liability cover before the first ride on an FSR. Almost every hunt starts on one.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ATV picture checklist. Helmet on every rider and passenger. Lights on from half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, and in poor visibility. Photo ID for everyone 12 and older. Under 16: an adult 19 or older supervises, no passengers. Spark arrestor in wildfire conditions.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Before you ride</text>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\">\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"190\" height=\"82\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"34\" width=\"190\" height=\"82\" rx=\"8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"122\" width=\"190\" height=\"82\" rx=\"8\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"122\" width=\"190\" height=\"82\" rx=\"8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"6\" y=\"210\" width=\"388\" height=\"84\" rx=\"8\"/>\n  </g>\n  <path d=\"M20 96 Q 20 52 54 52 Q 86 52 86 84 L86 96 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"56\" y=\"70\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"236\" cy=\"74\" r=\"18\" fill=\"#e8b10c\"/><g stroke=\"#e8b10c\" stroke-width=\"4\"><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"60\"/><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"274\" y2=\"74\"/><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"82\" x2=\"272\" y2=\"88\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"18\" y=\"140\" width=\"64\" height=\"44\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"36\" cy=\"158\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"152\" width=\"26\" height=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"50\" y=\"162\" width=\"20\" height=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"226\" cy=\"148\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"216\" y=\"160\" width=\"20\" height=\"30\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"160\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"255\" y=\"168\" width=\"14\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"236\" width=\"50\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><g fill=\"#e8590c\"><circle cx=\"82\" cy=\"244\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"238\" r=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"252\" r=\"3\"/></g><path d=\"M74 230 l26 30 M100 230 l-26 30\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"96\" y=\"70\">Helmet</text><text x=\"96\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">every rider</text>\n    <text x=\"280\" y=\"56\">Lights on</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">½ hr after sunset</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">to ½ hr before</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">sunrise</text>\n    <text x=\"92\" y=\"156\">Photo ID</text><text x=\"92\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">age 12 and up</text>\n    <text x=\"280\" y=\"152\">Under 16</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">adult 19+ near,</text><text x=\"280\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">no passengers</text>\n    <text x=\"116\" y=\"244\">Spark arrestor</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\">in wildfire conditions. $460 ticket</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Helmet on every rider and passenger on Crown land <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: standards, fines, the Synopsis quote</summary><ul><li>Helmet on every rider and passenger on a quad, dirt bike or snowmobile on Crown land <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Standards: Snell M2005 or M2010, FMVSS 218, or ECE 22 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><p>\"Mandatory safety laws apply to all ORVs; this includes helmets for ride-astride ORVs and seatbelts (if installed). People under 16 must be supervised by an adult at least 19 years.\" Synopsis page 9 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</p><ul><li>Lights on from half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, and any time weather cuts visibility <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Lights on for the ride out after legal light.</li><li>Everyone 12 and older carries government photo ID with a birthdate <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Under 16: supervised by an adult 19 or older who holds a driver's licence or a rider course certificate, and no passengers <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Careless operation, or harassing, running over or killing wildlife or livestock with an ORV: an offence, $368 ticket <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Spark arrestor required during wildfire conditions under the Wildfire Regulation. Ticket $460 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"3\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Guns and the quad in 3 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 3</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ATV gun step 1: at the truck, take the magazine out and empty the chamber, then put the rifle in the boot on the rack.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">At the truck: unload</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(200 196) scale(1.8)\"><rect x=\"-40\" y=\"-18\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"-46\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-6 -18 l6 -14 h10\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><rect x=\"150\" y=\"140\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" transform=\"rotate(-8 205 148)\"/><rect x=\"40\" y=\"70\" width=\"30\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Magazine out</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Chamber empty</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Magazine out, chamber empty, rifle in the boot</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> At the truck: magazine out, chamber empty.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ATV gun step 2: stop, turn the engine off, get off and step away from the quad.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stop. Get off. Step away.</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(110 196) scale(1.6)\"><rect x=\"-40\" y=\"-18\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"-46\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-6 -18 l6 -14 h10\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"150\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><path d=\"M180 150 h70 m-10 -8 l10 8 l-10 8\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tip: step away. Engine off is not enough</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Stop. Get off. Step away.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ATV gun step 3: load only once you are off and away from the quad, muzzle pointed a safe way. Hunt on foot, never from the seat or rack.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Load away from the quad</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(80 196) scale(1.4)\"><rect x=\"-40\" y=\"-18\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"-46\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"-26\" width=\"26\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"28\" cy=\"10\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M-6 -18 l6 -14 h10\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/></g><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"140\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"154\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"206\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"206\" x2=\"304\" y2=\"234\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><line x1=\"286\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Muzzle safe way</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Then hunt on foot. Never from the seat</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Load away from the quad. Hunt on foot.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>A loaded magazine clipped in = <strong>loaded</strong> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. An ATV is a motor vehicle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Never hunt from the seat or the rack <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the exact words</summary><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>Synopsis page 11, item 28 (2 October 2026 edition), exact words <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>: \"To discharge, carry or have in possession a firearm containing live ammunition in its breech or in its magazine attached to the firearm, in or on a railway car, motor vehicle, sleigh, aircraft, bicycle or other conveyance.\"</p></aside><ul><li>An ATV is a motor vehicle under the synopsis definition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Page 4.</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Loaded\">Loaded</button> in BC includes a loaded magazine clipped to the rifle <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Page 3. So: magazine out, chamber empty, before you touch the quad.</li><li>Item 22, page 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>: \"To hunt wildlife from a motor vehicle.\" Never from the seat, never from the rack.</li><li>Item 25, page 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>: no using a motor vehicle, power boat or aircraft to herd or harass wildlife.</li><li>Get off, step away from the quad, then load. Engine off is not enough <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. My reading of \"in or on\".</li><li>Tip: a padded rifle boot on the rack keeps dust out and the muzzle fixed. Bolt in your pocket on rough trails.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two kinds of closed area. Motor Vehicle Closed Area: no motor vehicle at all, or only some types such as ATVs. Motor Vehicle for Hunting Closed Area: no vehicle to hunt, or to carry game, gear or hunters. No sign is not a defence, the regulation wins.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two kinds of closed area</text>\n  <g>\n    <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"110\" r=\"64\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(100 116) scale(1.1)\"><rect x=\"-30\" y=\"-14\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-20\" cy=\"8\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"20\" cy=\"8\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n    <line x1=\"56\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"144\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"110\" r=\"64\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(286 122)\"><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"-12\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-17\" cy=\"7\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"7\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g>\n    <path d=\"M300 70 l20 0 l-6 16 h-10 Z M306 86 l10 26\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n    <line x1=\"256\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"344\" y2=\"154\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"10\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"200\">Motor Vehicle</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"218\">Closed Area</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"200\">Motor Vehicle for</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"218\">Hunting Closed Area</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"240\">no vehicle, or no ATVs</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"240\">no hunters, game, gear</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No sign is not a defence</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Signs may be missing. The regulation still wins <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the definitions</summary><ul><li>Two kinds under the Wildlife Act, each seasonal or year round <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Page 10.</li></ul><p>\"Motor Vehicle Closed Area: Prohibits the use or operation of a motor vehicle and e-bike. These prohibitions can be for all motor vehicles, or specific to ATVs/e-bikes or snowmobiles.\" Page 10 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</p><ul><li>Motor Vehicle for Hunting Closed Area: no vehicle to hunt, carry game, carry hunting gear or carry hunters to or from wildlife <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Closures include private land unless exempted. They do not include highways unless included <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Signs may be posted. Where sign and regulation differ, the regulation wins <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. No sign is not a defence <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Page 33.</li><li>The old name was Access Management Area. You will still hear it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Region 3 rule: above 1,700 metres, all motor vehicles except snowmobiles must stay on existing roads and trails. Below the line, other closures may still apply. No new tracks across the alpine.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Region 3: the 1,700 m line</text>\n  <path d=\"M0 270 L80 200 L150 120 L210 60 L270 110 L330 150 L400 210 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"0\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"400\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"10 6\"/>\n  <text x=\"10\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">1,700 m</text>\n  <path d=\"M60 260 Q 120 210 160 150 Q 190 110 210 64\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M232 92 Q 260 120 300 128\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <path d=\"M256 96 l20 20 M276 96 l-20 20\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">No new tracks</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Existing road</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"116\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">or trail only</text>\n  <text x=\"290\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Below: check your MU map</text>\n  <text x=\"290\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Snowmobiles excepted</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Above 1,700 m: existing roads and trails only <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Open the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit) closure map before you ride.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every Region 3 closure</summary><ul><li>Region 3 maps: <a href=\"https://www.gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gov.bc.ca/thompsonaccess</a>, a table of georeferenced PDF (Portable Document Format) maps by <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"MU\">MU</button> (Management Unit) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Region wide: \"The operation of all motor vehicles, excluding snowmobiles is prohibited in region 3 above 1,700 m elevation, except on existing roads and trails.\" Page 33 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Existing road or trail includes a logging road, and a trail bare enough that a 4 wheel vehicle can straddle any strip of plants <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Page 3. No new tracks across the alpine.</li><li>ATV for Hunting Closed: \"from Sept 1 - Dec 10 in MUs 3-28, 3-29, 3-30, and that portion of MU 3-17 shown on Map C3.\" Page 33 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. The regulation calls it Elephant Hills <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Skull Mountain (MU 3-28): closed 1 September to 10 December except roads shown open on Map C13 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li><li>Lac du Bois and Dewdrop (MUs 3-28, 3-29) and Dewdrop Rosseau Creek Wildlife Management Area (MU 3-29): closed year round except roads marked open <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Maps C15 and C16.</li><li>Greenstone Mountain Burn (MU 3-19): no vehicle for hunting except Duffy Lake Road, Beaton Lake Road and Greenstone Mountain Road <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. Map C5.</li><li>Stake Lake cross country ski trails: closed to unauthorized vehicles, motorbikes, ATVs and snowmobiles all year <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Date (2026)</th><th>Kamloops Fire Centre</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>10 August, noon</td><td>ORV ban in force</td><td><span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span></td></tr><tr><td>28 August</td><td>Ban lifted, news reports</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>25 September</td><td>No ORV ban listed</td><td><span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Check the fire centre page the night before every trip.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the details</summary><ul><li>BC Wildfire Service can ban recreational ORV use on Crown land across a whole fire centre <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>It happened in 2026: an ORV ban covered the Kamloops Fire Centre from noon on 10 August 2026 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">98%</span>. News reports say it was lifted on 28 August <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>On 25 September 2026 the Kamloops Fire Centre page listed no ORV ban and no area restrictions <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Area restriction orders close ground near active fires under Wildfire Act section 11 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Check the <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/safety/wildfire-status/prevention/fire-bans-and-restrictions/kamloops-fire-centre-bans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kamloops Fire Centre page</a> the night before every trip. Mission falls under a different fire centre: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> which.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"ATV on hills, rider course practice. Going up: low gear, weight forward. Going down: weight back. Never ride sideways across a steep slope. Stalled on a climb: brake, get off on the uphill side.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hills on a quad (Tip)</text>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M6 230 L126 120 L126 230 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(70 170) rotate(-42)\"><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"-12\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\"/><circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"4\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"4\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-12\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"-24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/></g>\n    <path d=\"M140 230 L260 230 L140 120 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(196 172) rotate(42)\"><rect x=\"-26\" y=\"-12\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\"/><circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"4\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"4\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"-4\" y1=\"-12\" x2=\"-12\" y2=\"-24\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/></g>\n    <path d=\"M274 230 L394 230 L394 150 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <g transform=\"translate(340 196)\"><rect x=\"-22\" y=\"-14\" width=\"44\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a5a3a\" transform=\"rotate(-30)\"/></g>\n    <path d=\"M318 170 l40 40 M358 170 l-40 40\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"256\">Up: lean</text><text x=\"66\" y=\"274\">forward</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"256\">Down: lean</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"274\">back</text><text x=\"334\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Never</text><text x=\"334\" y=\"274\" fill=\"#c0392b\">sideways</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stalled? Brake, get off uphill side</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Take a rider course. Ride with someone. Ride within your skill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: loads, trailering, roads</summary><ul><li>Take a rider course. Ride with someone. Ride within your skill <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>. Canada Safety Council code.</li><li>Hills: low gear, weight forward going up, weight back going down, never sideways across a steep slope <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Rider course practice.</li><li>Stalled on a climb: brake, dismount on the uphill side, never try to turn around on the slope <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Rider course practice.</li><li>Loads: rack limits are in the owner's manual and they are low. Heavy or high loads tip quads (Tip).</li><li>A deer on the rear rack: quarter it, strap it low and centred, head forward, and ride slower than you want to (Tip).</li><li>Quad on the truck: ramp straps on, then 4 ratchet straps to frame points, one per corner. Recheck after 10 minutes (Tip).</li><li>No alcohol. Lights on in dust. Slow for blind corners on FSRs. Logging trucks own the road (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"s2-atv-carry\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:0\"><span>ICBC registration certificate copy on the quad</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:1\"><span>Driver's licence and photo ID in my jacket</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:2\"><span>Proof of $200,000 liability insurance</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:3\"><span>Approved helmet, eye protection, gloves, boots over the ankle</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:4\"><span>Tow strap and a small tool kit</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:5\"><span>Tire plug kit and pump</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:6\"><span>Spare fuel if the loop is over half a tank</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:7\"><span>First aid kit, fire kit, headlamp, whistle</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:8\"><span>Water, food, extra warm layer</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:9\"><span>Spark arrestor fitted and checked</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:10\"><span>Region 3 closure maps for my MU downloaded offline</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s2-atv-carry:11\"><span>Is my ATV registered with ICBC? Plate on? If not, book the broker this week</span></label></div>","<aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): The quad gets you to the hunt. It is not the hunt. Park it, unload it, walk.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Loaded magazine clipped in on the rack. That is loaded.</li><li>Riding past a closure \"because the road was there\".</li><li>No liability insurance on the FSR.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>At the truck: magazine out, chamber empty, rifle in the boot. Helmet on. Say this MU's closure out loud before you turn the key.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Synopsis, ORV Act, regulations and ICBC read directly (95 to 99%). Riding tips: rider course practice (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: definitions pages 3 and 4, site and access restrictions page 9, motor vehicle prohibitions page 10, unlawful acts page 11, Region 3 page 33.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/14005\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Off Road Vehicle Act, SBC 2014 chapter 5</a>, BC Laws, current to 22 September 2026, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: sections 3, 14, 15, 17 to 20.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/193_2015\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Off Road Vehicle Regulation, B.C. Reg. 193/2015</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: sections 2, 4, 15 to 25 and the fee schedule.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.bclaws.gov.bc.ca/civix/document/id/complete/statreg/18_2024\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Motor Vehicle Prohibition Regulation, B.C. Reg. 18/2024</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: Schedule 1 items 7, 45 and 82, Schedule 2 item 49, Schedule 7 item 4.</li><li><a href=\"https://icbc.com/vehicle-registration/specialty-vehicles/Off-road-vehicles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ICBC off road vehicles page</a> and <a href=\"https://www.icbc.com/assets/en/2i7fcDxBUxk1cpQ63FAvkB/off-road-vehicle-plates.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ICBC Off Road Vehicle Plates, form MV1457</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/crown-land-water/crown-land/crown-land-uses/off-road-vehicles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC off road vehicles page</a> and its <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/industry/crown-land-water/crown-land/crown-land-uses/off-road-vehicles/safety\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">safety page</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: fines, spark arrestor, photo ID.</li><li><a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/sports-culture/recreation/motor-vehicle-prohibitions/region-3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Motor Vehicle Prohibitions, Region 3</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01.</li><li><a href=\"https://blog.gov.bc.ca/bcwildfire/off-road-vehicles-to-be-prohibited-in-the-kamloops-fire-centre/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">BC Wildfire Service blog, ORV prohibition in the Kamloops Fire Centre</a> and the <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/safety/wildfire-status/prevention/fire-bans-and-restrictions/kamloops-fire-centre-bans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Kamloops Fire Centre prohibitions page</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01. The lifting date comes from news search previews <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.for.gov.bc.ca/mof/orv/qa_orv_act.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ministry ORV Act FAQ, October 2015</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01: highway versus FSR, permits.</li><li><a href=\"https://canadasafetycouncil.org/safety-code-for-atv-riders/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Canada Safety Council, Safety Code for ATV Riders</a> and <a href=\"https://www.adventuresmart.ca/off-road-vehicle/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AdventureSmart, Off road vehicle</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01. Hill, load and tie down lines are rider course practice, labelled Tip.</li></ul></details>"]